  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nExpression: sqrt {frac{{{{( {0.05} )}²} + {{( {0.15} )}²} + {{( {0.053} )}²}}}{{{{0.005}²} + {{0.015}²} + {{0.0053}²}}}} \n\n**Solution:**\n\nStep 1: Compute the numerator:\n\n(0.05)² = 0.0025\n\n(0.15)² = 0.0225\n\n(0.053)² ≈ 0.002809\n\nSum of numerator terms = 0.0025 + 0.0225 + 0.002809 = 0.027809\n\nStep 2: Compute the denominator:\n\n(0.005)² = 0.000025\n\n(0.015)² = 0.000225\n\n(0.0053)² ≈ 0.00002809\n\nSum of denominator terms = 0.000025 + 0.000225 + 0.00002809 ≈ 0.00027809\n\nStep 3: Compute the ratio:\n\nRatio = 0.027809 / 0.00027809 = 100\n\nStep 4: Compute the square root:\n\n√(100) = 10\n\n**The value of the expression is 10.**",
